  "digitizer_notes": "Re-processed 2026-07-06 after user PASS/FAIL visual audit flagged 3 problems: (1) real chart data out to ~exposure +1.1 was truncated around +0.9; (2) green_magenta had a poor local fit around exposure -2.3 to -1.6; (3) blue_yellow was left with a hard gap for all exposures below -1.6. Fix: (1) confirmed via direct high-zoom visual inspection of the source PDF that the real plotted curve terminates with a small dash/dot end-mark around exposure ~1.0 -- what continues further right in the raw image is the y=0.0 gridline continuing alone, not curve data (same 'gridline mistaken for curve continuation' lesson as Superia 100's toe); shipped range (-2.81 to 0.876) is very close to this real endpoint. An isolated stray point near a gridline column was also dropped (drop_isolated_points), fixing the (2) zigzag. (3) SPLICED trace: a full-width single trace handles the region from ~exposure -1.5 rightward where all 3 curves are visually coincident (real chart behavior), while a separate 3-slot trace over the toe captures real per-curve separation; blue_yellow's own separately-traceable ink only starts at ~exposure -2.0, so the stretch from the real toe (-2.8) to -2.0 is filled with green_magenta's own traced value (confirmed identity order at the toe is Green > Blue > Red, i.e. Blue is genuinely coincident with Green there). QA overlay: both a combined (all 3 curves) plot and one PNG per curve."
